      "time": "~40s",
      "narrative": "Relying on the model's training alone would only give me generic results. But I want this agent to operate like a member of my team, with all the context and unique IQ that we have in house. \n\nI quickly connect it to Work IQ, Fabric IQ, SharePoint, and Teams. \n\nNow the agent reasons over Caldova's contracts, supplier data, and operating context.\n\nIts recommendations are grounded in the unique knowledge, insights and data of the business, not just the model. \n\nAnd notice the choice: which model, which knowledge, which surface. That's the platform point — this is open, not a single locked destination. ",
      "demo_actions": "Show the configured enterprise connections and tool access in VS Code. Call out WorkIQ, FabricIQ, SharePoint, and Teams as knowledge sources the agent can use during reasoning.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260622_142605_vlcsnap-2026-06-22-14h25m58s345.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
